    "id": "b10a0852126775f2b57b627c",
    "path": "buoyant_kernel::snapshot::builder::IncrementalReplay",
    "name": "IncrementalReplay",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "buoyant_kernel",
    "version": "1.0.0+58f07cd6",
    "kind": "enum",
    "signature": "enum IncrementalReplay",
    "docs": "Controls whether kernel replays commits to advance a stale base CRC (the existing snapshot's\nin-memory CRC, or an on-disk CRC) to the target snapshot version on load. A CRC already at the\ntarget version is always used regardless of this setting; this only bounds the cost of\nadvancing a *stale* CRC.\n\nA resolved CRC gives the snapshot precomputed file statistics (file count and sizes, useful\nfor query optimization and for writers producing a post-commit CRC) along with domain metadata\nand set transactions (useful for writers), all without extra log replay.",
